  savedPlayerHealth: 0
  loadingTips:
  - Unique tools can be repaired with souls in the inventory.
  - Unique tools can be found on some islands and can be unlocked for 150 souls each.
  - Some monsters drop soul fragments which can be spent to upgrade stats in the
    inventory.
  - The ominous flower is crafted with a soul fragment from each biome.
  - 'Fun fact: I made this game.'
  - Rocks do more damage and are better at breaking things than your fist alone.
  - The boat constructor creates boats which can travel to new islands.
  - The battleship can destroy ocean rocks with its missile launcher.
  - Uranium tools are better than tungsten tools but they have less durability.
  - It takes 150 souls to unlock a unique tool once you find it.
  - This loading screen takes way too long...
  - Recalling while you are the only one on a boat brings the boat to the island
    with you.
  - When the plane crashed on the island, the cockpit was swallowed by a mysterious
    red puddle.
  - Looks like you and the people playing with you were the only survivors of the
    plane crash.
  - In eldritch mode you can't respawn after dying.
  - Uranium-235 chunks have to be purified in a uranium purifier before they can
    be used.
  - Enemies aren't scared of water anymore on hard mode and above.
  - If you drown you will be sent back to your spawn point and lose some health.
  - Enemies can't spawn on floors - make sure to add them in your base.
  - In the volcanic caves, enemies spawn even during the day.
  - Crops don't need to be watered during rain.
  - The soul tracker won't light up if the unique tool on your island has already
    been claimed.
  - Don't put an onion in the uranium purifier...
  - "\U0001F62D\U0001F494\U0001F64F\U0001F62D\U0001F63F"
